WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.640
- [Narrator] Seeing a nearly 50 percent decrease

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.170
in population over the past decade,

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:08.253
this is the radiated tortoise.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.930
Endemic to the dry southern
forests of Madagascar,

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:20.340
the radiated tortoise has
an amazingly long lifespan.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.090
The oldest tortoise on record

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:25.303
reached an estimated 188 years old.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.200
Their shell is domed and highly intricate,

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.980
with bright yellow star patterns

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.970
radiating outwards on each plate.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.740
The shells have both
blood vessels and nerves.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.353
Meaning that it can feel
when it's being touched.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.040
The sharp decline in the
tortoise's population

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.490
is mostly due to hunting and
the black market pet trade.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:50.030
In Madagascar, their meat
is considered a delicacy

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:54.250
and illegal poaching has
decimated wild populations.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.890
Additionally, their distinctive
markings on their shells

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.023
have made them desirably as pets.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.030
It's estimated that a staggering

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:03.865
quarter-of-a-million radiated tortoises

00:01:03.865 --> 00:01:06.510
are harvested each year.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:08.700
Conservationists estimate these animals

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.340
could go extinct in less than 20 years.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.763
This is the radiated tortoise.

